module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Descent.IsStack.SingletonGluing
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.TwoYoneda.RepresentedPoint

/-!
# A gluing system from a family of morphisms of the values of a 2-Yoneda functor

Let `p : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒞` be fibred in groupoids, let `q : U₀ ⟶ Ū` be an arrow of the base and let `ξ` be an
object of the fibre over `U₀`. By the 2-Yoneda lemma (**Stacks 004B**) `ξ` is named by a functor
`G : 𝒞/U₀ ⥤ 𝒳` over `𝒞`, whose value at the object `(Z, ε)` of the slice is a cartesian lift of
`ε` at `ξ` — a pullback `ε^* ξ`, but the one `G` chose rather than the one a prefibered structure
chose.

`CategoryTheory.Functor.exists_iso_pullbackFiber_of_gluing_generate` descends `ξ` along `q` from a
**gluing system**: a family of isomorphisms `θ ε ε' : ε^* ξ ≅ ε'^* ξ` between the *chosen*
pullbacks, one for each pair of arrows into `U₀` agreeing after `q`, composing and compatible with
base change. This file produces such a system from the corresponding family on the values of `G`,
where both conditions take a shape a geometric construction can supply: a family

`Θ ε ε' : G(Z, ε) ⟶ G(Z, ε')`

of morphisms of the fibre over `Z`, composing, and commuting with the restriction morphisms
`G(Z', γ ≫ ε) ⟶ G(Z, ε)` that `G` itself supplies. No inverse is asked of `Θ`: the fibres of `p`
are groupoids.

The translation is two comparison isomorphisms and one identity between them. The value of `G` at
`(Z, ε)` is compared with the chosen pullback `ε^* ξ` by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso`, both being cartesian lifts of `ε` at `ξ`,
and the chosen pullback along `γ` of that value is compared with the value at `(Z', γ ≫ ε)` by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceRestrictIso`, both being cartesian lifts of `γ` at it. The
identity `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict` says the two comparisons
agree with the contraction of the iterated chosen pullback, and it is what turns compatibility of
`Θ` with restriction into compatibility of `θ` with base change.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceRestrict`: the restriction morphism of `G` along an arrow
  of the base.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceRestrictIso`: the chosen pullback along `γ` of a value of
  `G`, compared with the value of `G` at the composite.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceToPoint`: the cartesian lift of `ε` at `ξ` that `G`
  supplies at `(Z, ε)`.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso`: the chosen pullback `ε^* ξ`, compared
  with the value of `G` at `(Z, ε)`.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceGluingIso`: **the gluing isomorphism of a family `Θ`.**

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict`: the two comparisons agree with
  the contraction of an iterated chosen pullback.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceRestrictIso_conj_sq` and
  `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceRestrictIso_conj`: the base change of a morphism of the
  values of `G`, read through the comparisons, commutes with the restriction morphisms, and is the
  only morphism that does.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceGluingIso_trans` and
  `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceGluingIso_pullback`: the two conditions of a gluing
  system, for the family of gluing isomorphisms of `Θ`.
* `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.exists_iso_pullbackFiber_of_sliceGluing`: **a composing,
  restriction-compatible family `Θ` descends `ξ` along `q`** when `p` is a stack and the sieve
  generated by `q` covers.

## Implementation notes

Every identity below is stated between morphisms of one fibre and proved by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.fiber_hom_ext_of_cartesian` against one of the three cartesian lifts in
play — the chosen `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsPreFibered.pullbackMap`, the restriction morphism of
`G`, and the lift of `ε` at `ξ` that `G` supplies. Each comparison is pinned down by its composite
with the lifts it compares, exactly as the comparisons of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Descent.IsStack.PullbackFiberComp` are, and the rest is algebra
of isomorphisms of a fibre.

`CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceObjFiber` of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.TwoYoneda.PullbackComparison` is the value of `G` read in the fibre,
and `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceToTerminal` the arrow of the slice to its terminal
object; the restriction morphism along `γ` is `G` applied to `Over.homMk γ`, and the two are
related by the uniqueness of an arrow to a terminal object, which is where
`CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceToPoint_comp` comes from.

The prefibered structure enters only through `pullbackFiber`, so it is taken as an instance
argument rather than drawn from the hypothesis that `p` is fibred in groupoids, which is itself an
explicit argument of every declaration using it rather than a section variable.

`CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.isHomLift_sliceToPoint` supplies the two lifting conditions of
`CategoryTheory.IsHomLift.comp_lift_id_right'` positionally: the object of `𝒳` through which the
composite factors is written as a value of `G` on one side of that application and as the value of
2-Yoneda evaluation on the other, and those agree only at default transparency, which instance
search does not use.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 004B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/004B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 026B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/026B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 026F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/026F)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace CategoryTheory

open Limits Opposite

universe v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂

namespace Functor.TwoYoneda

variable {𝒞 : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} 𝒞] {𝒳 : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} 𝒳]

variable {p : 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒞} {U₀ : 𝒞}
  {G : BasedCategory.ofFunctor (Over.forget U₀) ⥤ᵇ BasedCategory.ofFunctor p}

/-! ### The restriction morphisms of a functor on a slice -/

/-- The restriction morphism of a functor over `𝒞` on the slice `𝒞/U₀` along `γ : Z' ⟶ Z`: its
image of the arrow `(Z', γ ≫ ε) ⟶ (Z, ε)` of the slice given by `γ`. -/
def sliceRestrict {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    (sliceObjFiber p (γ ≫ ε) G).1 ⟶ (sliceObjFiber p ε G).1 :=
  G.map (Over.homMk γ : (Over.mk (γ ≫ ε) : Over U₀) ⟶ Over.mk ε)

/-- The restriction morphism lies over `γ`. -/
lemma isHomLift_sliceRestrict {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    p.IsHomLift γ (sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ) := by
  let φ : (Over.mk (γ ≫ ε) : Over U₀) ⟶ Over.mk ε := Over.homMk γ
  have : (BasedCategory.ofFunctor (Over.forget U₀)).p.IsHomLift γ φ :=
    IsHomLift.map (p := Over.forget U₀) φ
  exact BasedFunctor.preserves_isHomLift G γ φ

/-- The restriction morphism is a cartesian lift of `γ`: in a category fibred in groupoids every
morphism lying over an arrow of the base is strongly cartesian. -/
lemma isCartesian_sliceRestrict (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀)
    (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) : p.IsCartesian γ (sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ) := by
  have := isHomLift_sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ
  have := hp.isStronglyCartesian_homLift γ (sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ)
  infer_instance

/-- **The chosen pullback along `γ` of the value of `G` at `(Z, ε)`, compared with the value of `G`
at `(Z', γ ≫ ε)`**: both carry a cartesian morphism over `γ` to the first value. -/
noncomputable def sliceRestrictIso [p.IsPreFibered] (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z Z' : 𝒞}
    (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    pullbackFiber p (sliceObjFiber p ε G) γ ≅ sliceObjFiber p (γ ≫ ε) G :=
  fiberIsoOfCartesian γ (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (sliceObjFiber p ε G).2 γ)
    (sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ) (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap.IsCartesian _ _)
    (isCartesian_sliceRestrict hp ε γ)

/-- The comparison followed by the restriction morphism is the chosen cartesian lift. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma sliceRestrictIso_hom_fac [p.IsPreFibered] (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z Z' : 𝒞}
    (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).hom ≫
        sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ =
      IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (sliceObjFiber p ε G).2 γ :=
  fiberIsoOfCartesian_hom_fac _ _ _ _ _

/-- The inverse comparison followed by the chosen cartesian lift is the restriction morphism. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma sliceRestrictIso_inv_fac [p.IsPreFibered] (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z Z' : 𝒞}
    (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).inv ≫
        IsPreFibered.pullbackMap (sliceObjFiber p ε G).2 γ = sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ :=
  fiberIsoOfCartesian_inv_fac _ _ _ _ _

/-- Three composable morphisms of a fibre, mapped into the total category, whose composite with a
morphism `s` is computed by successively rewriting the last morphism. -/
private theorem fiberInclusion_map_comp_comp_comp_eq {Z : 𝒞} {A B C D : p.Fiber Z} {V : 𝒳}
    {a : A ⟶ B} {b : B ⟶ C} {c : C ⟶ D} {s : D.1 ⟶ V} {X : C.1 ⟶ V} {Y : B.1 ⟶ V}
    {w : A.1 ⟶ V} (hc : Fiber.fiberInclusion.map c ≫ s = X)
    (hb : Fiber.fiberInclusion.map b ≫ X = Y) (ha : Fiber.fiberInclusion.map a ≫ Y = w) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (a ≫ b ≫ c) ≫ s = w := by
  rw [Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp]
  erw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hc, hb, ha]

/-- **The base change along `γ` of a morphism of the values of `G`, read through the comparison
isomorphisms, commutes with the restriction morphisms along `γ`.** -/
lemma sliceRestrictIso_conj_sq [p.IsPreFibered] (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z Z' : 𝒞}
    (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) (η : sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map ((sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).inv ≫
          pullbackFiberHom η γ ≫ (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε' γ).hom) ≫
        sliceRestrict (G := G) ε' γ =
      sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map η :=
  fiberInclusion_map_comp_comp_comp_eq (sliceRestrictIso_hom_fac hp ε' γ)
    (pullbackFiberHom_fac η γ)
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans (sliceRestrictIso_inv_fac_assoc hp ε γ _))

/-- **A morphism of the values of `G` commuting with the restriction morphisms is the base change
of the one it commutes with**, read through the comparison isomorphisms. Both sides are pinned
down by their composite with the restriction morphism out of the target. -/
lemma sliceRestrictIso_conj [p.IsPreFibered] (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z Z' : 𝒞}
    (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) (η : sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G)
    (η' : sliceObjFiber p (γ ≫ ε) G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p (γ ≫ ε') G)
    (hsq : Fiber.fiberInclusion.map η' ≫ sliceRestrict (G := G) ε' γ =
      sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map η) :
    (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).inv ≫ pullbackFiberHom η γ ≫
        (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε' γ).hom = η' :=
  fiber_hom_ext_of_cartesian γ (sliceRestrict (G := G) ε' γ)
    (isCartesian_sliceRestrict hp ε' γ) _ _
    ((sliceRestrictIso_conj_sq hp ε ε' γ η).trans hsq.symm)

/-! ### The cartesian lift of `ε` at `ξ` that `G` supplies -/

/-- The cartesian lift of `ε` at `ξ` that `G` supplies at the object `(Z, ε)` of the slice: the
image of the arrow to the terminal object, followed by the comparison of the value there
with `ξ`. -/
noncomputable def sliceToPoint {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) {Z : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) :
    (sliceObjFiber p ε G).1 ⟶ ξ.1 :=
  G.map (sliceToTerminal ε) ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map e.hom

/-- `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceToPoint` lies over `ε`. -/
lemma isHomLift_sliceToPoint {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) {Z : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) :
    p.IsHomLift ε (sliceToPoint e ε) :=
  have h0 : p.IsHomLift ε (G.map (sliceToTerminal ε)) :=
    Functor.TwoYoneda.isHomLift_map_from_mkIdTerminal p U₀ G (Over.mk ε)
  have h1 : p.IsHomLift (𝟙 U₀) (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map e.hom) := e.hom.2
  @IsHomLift.comp_lift_id_right' _ _ _ _ p _ _ _ _ _ ε (G.map (sliceToTerminal ε)) h0 U₀
    (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map e.hom) h1

/-- `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceToPoint` is a strongly cartesian lift of `ε`: in a
category fibred in groupoids every morphism lying over an arrow of the base is. -/
lemma isStronglyCartesian_sliceToPoint (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) {Z : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) :
    p.IsStronglyCartesian ε (sliceToPoint e ε) :=
  have := isHomLift_sliceToPoint e ε
  hp.isStronglyCartesian_homLift ε (sliceToPoint e ε)

/-- `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceToPoint` is a cartesian lift of `ε`. -/
lemma isCartesian_sliceToPoint (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) {Z : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) :
    p.IsCartesian ε (sliceToPoint e ε) := by
  have := isStronglyCartesian_sliceToPoint hp e ε
  infer_instance

/-- The cartesian lift of `γ ≫ ε` that `G` supplies is the restriction morphism along `γ` followed
by the cartesian lift of `ε`: the arrow of the slice to the terminal object out of `(Z', γ ≫ ε)` is
the only one there is, so it factors through the arrow given by `γ`. -/
lemma sliceToPoint_comp {ξ : p.Fiber U₀} (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ)
    {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    sliceToPoint e (γ ≫ ε) = sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ ≫ sliceToPoint e ε :=
  have hfac : (Over.homMk γ : (Over.mk (γ ≫ ε) : Over U₀) ⟶ Over.mk ε) ≫ sliceToTerminal ε =
      sliceToTerminal (γ ≫ ε) := Over.mkIdTerminal.hom_ext _ _
  have hmap : G.map (sliceToTerminal (γ ≫ ε)) =
      sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ ≫ G.map (sliceToTerminal ε) :=
    (congrArg G.toFunctor.map hfac).symm.trans (G.toFunctor.map_comp _ _)
  (congrArg (fun m => m ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map e.hom) hmap).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _)

/-! ### The chosen pullback compared with the value of `G` -/

/-- **The chosen pullback of `ξ` along `ε`, compared with the value of `G` at `(Z, ε)`**: both
carry a cartesian morphism over `ε` to `ξ`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackFiberSliceIso [p.IsPreFibered] {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z : 𝒞}
    (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) : pullbackFiber p ξ ε ≅ sliceObjFiber p ε G :=
  fiberIsoOfCartesian ε (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap ξ.2 ε) (sliceToPoint e ε)
    (IsPreFibered.pullbackMap.IsCartesian _ _) (isCartesian_sliceToPoint hp e ε)

/-- The comparison followed by the cartesian lift `G` supplies is the chosen cartesian lift. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma pullbackFiberSliceIso_hom_fac [p.IsPreFibered] {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z : 𝒞}
    (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).hom ≫ sliceToPoint e ε =
      IsPreFibered.pullbackMap ξ.2 ε :=
  fiberIsoOfCartesian_hom_fac _ _ _ _ _

/-- The inverse comparison followed by the chosen cartesian lift is the lift `G` supplies. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma pullbackFiberSliceIso_inv_fac [p.IsPreFibered] {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) {Z : 𝒞}
    (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) :
    Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).inv ≫
        IsPreFibered.pullbackMap ξ.2 ε = sliceToPoint e ε :=
  fiberIsoOfCartesian_inv_fac _ _ _ _ _

/-- **The two comparisons agree with the contraction of an iterated chosen pullback.** This is the
identity that turns compatibility of a family with restriction into compatibility of its gluing
isomorphisms with base change. -/
lemma pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict [p.IsFibered] {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    (pullbackFiberCompIso ξ ε γ).inv ≫
        pullbackFiberHom (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).hom γ ≫
          (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).hom =
      (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp (γ ≫ ε)).hom := by
  refine fiber_hom_ext_of_cartesian (γ ≫ ε) (sliceToPoint e (γ ≫ ε))
    (isCartesian_sliceToPoint hp e (γ ≫ ε)) _ _ ?_
  rw [pullbackFiberSliceIso_hom_fac]
  exact fiberInclusion_map_comp_comp_comp_eq
    ((congrArg (Fiber.fiberInclusion.map _ ≫ ·) (sliceToPoint_comp e ε γ)).trans
      ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans (sliceRestrictIso_hom_fac_assoc hp ε γ _)))
    ((pullbackFiberHom_fac_assoc _ γ _).trans
      (congrArg (_ ≫ ·) (pullbackFiberSliceIso_hom_fac e hp ε)))
    (pullbackFiberCompIso_inv_fac ξ ε γ)

/-- `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict` solved for the contraction
followed by the base change of the comparison. -/
lemma pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict' [p.IsFibered] {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    (pullbackFiberCompIso ξ ε γ).inv ≫ pullbackFiberHom (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).hom γ =
      (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp (γ ≫ ε)).hom ≫ (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).inv := by
  rw [Iso.eq_comp_inv, Category.assoc, pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict]

/-- `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict` solved for the base change of
the inverse comparison followed by the contraction. -/
lemma pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict_inv [p.IsFibered] {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε : Z ⟶ U₀) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    pullbackFiberHom (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).inv γ ≫ (pullbackFiberCompIso ξ ε γ).hom =
      (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).hom ≫ (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp (γ ≫ ε)).inv :=
  have h : (pullbackFiberCompIso ξ ε γ).symm ≪≫
        pullbackFiberIso (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε) γ =
      (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp (γ ≫ ε)) ≪≫ (sliceRestrictIso (G := G) hp ε γ).symm :=
    Iso.ext (pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict' e hp ε γ)
  congrArg Iso.hom (congrArg Iso.symm h)

/-! ### The gluing system -/

/-- **The gluing isomorphism attached to a family of morphisms of the values of `G`.** No inverse
is asked of the family: a morphism of a fibre of a category fibred in groupoids is an
isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def sliceGluingIso [p.IsFibered] {Ū : 𝒞} {q : U₀ ⟶ Ū} {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (Θ : ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀), ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q →
      (sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G))
    {Z : 𝒞} (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (h : ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q) :
    pullbackFiber p ξ ε ≅ pullbackFiber p ξ ε' :=
  have := hp.fiber_isGroupoid Z
  have : IsIso (Θ ε ε' h) := IsGroupoid.all_isIso _
  (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).trans
    ((asIso (Θ ε ε' h)).trans (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε').symm)

/-- The forward direction of the gluing isomorphism, written out. -/
lemma sliceGluingIso_hom [p.IsFibered] {Ū : 𝒞} {q : U₀ ⟶ Ū} {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (Θ : ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀), ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q →
      (sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G))
    {Z : 𝒞} (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (h : ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q) :
    (sliceGluingIso e hp Θ ε ε' h).hom =
      (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε).hom ≫ Θ ε ε' h ≫ (pullbackFiberSliceIso e hp ε').inv :=
  rfl

/-- **The cocycle condition of the gluing system**, from the composition law of the family: the
two inner comparisons cancel. -/
lemma sliceGluingIso_trans [p.IsFibered] {Ū : 𝒞} {q : U₀ ⟶ Ū} {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (Θ : ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀), ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q →
      (sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G))
    (hΘ : ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ : Z ⟶ U₀) (h₁₂ : ε₁ ≫ q = ε₂ ≫ q) (h₂₃ : ε₂ ≫ q = ε₃ ≫ q)
      (h₁₃ : ε₁ ≫ q = ε₃ ≫ q), Θ ε₁ ε₂ h₁₂ ≫ Θ ε₂ ε₃ h₂₃ = Θ ε₁ ε₃ h₁₃)
    {Z : 𝒞} (ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ : Z ⟶ U₀) (h₁₂ : ε₁ ≫ q = ε₂ ≫ q) (h₂₃ : ε₂ ≫ q = ε₃ ≫ q)
    (h₁₃ : ε₁ ≫ q = ε₃ ≫ q) :
    (sliceGluingIso e hp Θ ε₁ ε₂ h₁₂).hom ≫ (sliceGluingIso e hp Θ ε₂ ε₃ h₂₃).hom =
      (sliceGluingIso e hp Θ ε₁ ε₃ h₁₃).hom := by
  rw [sliceGluingIso_hom, sliceGluingIso_hom, sliceGluingIso_hom,
    ← hΘ ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ h₁₂ h₂₃ h₁₃]
  simp only [Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

/-- **Compatibility of the gluing system with base change**, from compatibility of the family with
the restriction morphisms of `G`: the two contractions are carried to those restriction morphisms
by `CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict`, and
`CategoryTheory.Functor.TwoYoneda.sliceRestrictIso_conj` then recognises the conjugated base change
as the member of the family at the restricted pair. -/
lemma sliceGluingIso_pullback [p.IsFibered] {Ū : 𝒞} {q : U₀ ⟶ Ū} {ξ : p.Fiber U₀}
    (e : (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (Θ : ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀), ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q →
      (sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G))
    (hΘpull : ∀ ⦃Z Z' : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (h : ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z)
      (h' : (γ ≫ ε) ≫ q = (γ ≫ ε') ≫ q),
      Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (Θ (γ ≫ ε) (γ ≫ ε') h') ≫ sliceRestrict (G := G) ε' γ =
        sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (Θ ε ε' h))
    {Z Z' : 𝒞} (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (h : ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z) :
    (pullbackFiberCompIso ξ ε γ).inv ≫
        pullbackFiberHom (sliceGluingIso e hp Θ ε ε' h).hom γ ≫
          (pullbackFiberCompIso ξ ε' γ).hom =
      (sliceGluingIso e hp Θ (γ ≫ ε) (γ ≫ ε')
        (by rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, h])).hom := by
  have hconj := sliceRestrictIso_conj (G := G) hp ε ε' γ (Θ ε ε' h)
    (Θ (γ ≫ ε) (γ ≫ ε') (by rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, h]))
    (hΘpull ε ε' h γ (by rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, h]))
  rw [sliceGluingIso_hom, sliceGluingIso_hom, ← hconj, pullbackFiberHom_comp,
    pullbackFiberHom_comp]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict_inv e hp ε' γ, ← Category.assoc,
    pullbackFiberSliceIso_restrict' e hp ε γ]
  simp only [Category.assoc]

/-- **A composing, restriction-compatible family of morphisms of the values of `G` descends `ξ`
along `q`.** Let `p` be a stack over `(𝒞, J)` fibred in groupoids, let `q : U₀ ⟶ Ū` generate a
covering sieve of `Ū`, let `ξ` be an object of the fibre over `U₀` and `G` a functor over `𝒞` on
the slice `𝒞/U₀` naming it. A family of morphisms of the values of `G` at the pairs of arrows into
`U₀` agreeing after `q`, composing and commuting with the restriction morphisms of `G`, makes `ξ`
the pullback along `q` of an object of the fibre over `Ū`. -/
theorem exists_iso_pullbackFiber_of_sliceGluing {J : GrothendieckTopology 𝒞} {Ū : 𝒞}
    {q : U₀ ⟶ Ū} {ξ : p.Fiber U₀} (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hstack : p.IsStack J)
    (e : haveI := hstack.isFibered
      (Functor.twoYonedaEvaluation p U₀).obj G ≅ ξ)
    (hq : Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton q) ∈ J Ū)
    (Θ : haveI := hstack.isFibered
      ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀), ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q →
        (sliceObjFiber p ε G ⟶ sliceObjFiber p ε' G))
    (hΘ : haveI := hstack.isFibered
      ∀ ⦃Z : 𝒞⦄ (ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ : Z ⟶ U₀) (h₁₂ : ε₁ ≫ q = ε₂ ≫ q) (h₂₃ : ε₂ ≫ q = ε₃ ≫ q)
        (h₁₃ : ε₁ ≫ q = ε₃ ≫ q), Θ ε₁ ε₂ h₁₂ ≫ Θ ε₂ ε₃ h₂₃ = Θ ε₁ ε₃ h₁₃)
    (hΘpull : haveI := hstack.isFibered
      ∀ ⦃Z Z' : 𝒞⦄ (ε ε' : Z ⟶ U₀) (h : ε ≫ q = ε' ≫ q) (γ : Z' ⟶ Z)
        (h' : (γ ≫ ε) ≫ q = (γ ≫ ε') ≫ q),
        Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (Θ (γ ≫ ε) (γ ≫ ε') h') ≫ sliceRestrict (G := G) ε' γ =
          sliceRestrict (G := G) ε γ ≫ Fiber.fiberInclusion.map (Θ ε ε' h)) :
    haveI := hstack.isFibered
    ∃ x : p.Fiber Ū, Nonempty (ξ ≅ pullbackFiber p x q) := by
  have := hstack.isFibered
  exact Functor.exists_iso_pullbackFiber_of_gluing_generate hstack q hq ξ
    (fun ⦃_⦄ ε ε' hh => sliceGluingIso e hp Θ ε ε' hh)
    (fun ⦃_⦄ ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ h₁₂ h₂₃ h₁₃ => sliceGluingIso_trans e hp Θ hΘ ε₁ ε₂ ε₃ h₁₂ h₂₃ h₁₃)
    (fun ⦃_ _⦄ ε ε' hh γ => sliceGluingIso_pullback e hp Θ hΘpull ε ε' hh γ)

end Functor.TwoYoneda

end CategoryTheory

